Exporters & Targets in Prometheus

🔹 What are Targets? 🎯
 Targets are the systems or applications from which Prometheus collects metrics.
 👉 These can be servers, containers, APIs, or services.

🔹 What are Exporters? 📦
 Exporters act as data translators.
 They convert system or application data into a Prometheus-readable format.
👉 Flow:
 Application/System → Exporter → Prometheus

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 Most systems don’t expose metrics in Prometheus format by default.
 👉 Exporters make it possible to monitor everything 🚀

🔹 Node Exporter (Infrastructure Monitoring) 🖥️
✔ Used to monitor server-level metrics
 ✔ Provides:
CPU usage
Memory usage
Disk usage
Network stats
👉 Example:
 Monitor EC2/Linux server health

🔹 Application Metrics 🚀
✔ Metrics generated by your application
 ✔ Examples:
Request count
Error rate
Response time
👉 Apps expose metrics via /metrics endpoint

🔹 Real-world Usage: 💡
You have a web application running on a server
👉 Node Exporter collects:
CPU = 85%
Memory = 70%
👉 Application exposes:
Requests/sec
Error rate
👉 Prometheus pulls all data
 👉 If error rate increases 🚨 → Alert triggered

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Targets = Data sources 🎯
 ✔ Exporters = Data converters 📦
 ✔ Node Exporter = Server metrics 🖥️
 ✔ App metrics = Business performance 🚀
 ✔ Together = Complete visibility
